  "step_3": "The decision reason is based on skewness — specifically, preferring a lottery that is more right-skewed, meaning a greater portion of probability is on unfavorable outcomes. However, both lotteries have nearly all their probability (over 99%) on the 0 Euro outcome, so both are equally right-skewed in terms of probability distribution. The individual does not mention skewness, probability distribution, or any comparison of unfavorable vs favorable outcomes. Instead, the individual focuses on the size of the potential gain, dismissing the probability difference as negligible. Therefore, the individual did not consider or apply the skewness-based decision reason. The justification is based on the amount of money won, not on the shape of the probability distribution. Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
